[KiCad-IOS port] Round 23: a crash-surviving stage breadcrumb
channel -- PATHS::IosBreadcrumb() appends one line per stage to
Documents/kicad-ios-breadcrumb.log.

Why (hidden_files/round23-bug-ledger.md, diagnostic-channel
finding): every stage trace this port has shipped uses
wxLogTrace on the "KICAD_IOS" channel. That mask is never
enabled at runtime -- no AddTraceMask call exists in KiCad's
init or in any port patch, the advanced-config TraceMasks
default is empty, and the WXTRACE route needs a debug build
plus an environment variable a sideloaded iOS app cannot have.
The default log target on this wxQt build forwards trace
records to stderr, i.e. the iOS unified log, which nobody
retrieved. Round 22's chooser stage traces
(round22-chooser-3d-skipped / round22-fpchooser-frame-ready)
were therefore unobservable on device even if reached: the
round flew blind and the gate could only prove the literals
were compiled in, not where execution died.

Fix: a direct file channel that bypasses wxLog entirely.
PATHS::IosBreadcrumb(const char*) is declared in include/paths.h
and implemented in common/paths.cpp (both compiled into
libkicommon, which already carries KICAD_IOS_PORT via patch
0032 and is linked by every kiface, so eeschema, pcbnew and
common callers share one implementation). On iOS it appends
"<unix-time> <stage>\n" to
KIPLATFORM::ENV::GetDocumentsPath() +
"/kicad-ios-breadcrumb.log" -- the root of the app's Documents
folder, user-retrievable via Files -> On My iPad -> KiCad
(file sharing is enabled in the bundle by
scripts/package_ios.py). Every call opens, writes, fflushes,
fsyncs and closes: a buffered line in a long-lived handle
would die with the process in a hard crash; a closed line
survives. Off iOS the function is a no-op. kicad/kicad.cpp
writes "round23-session-start" at startup (next to patch
0034's Documents working-directory fix) to delimit runs in
the append-only file.

Stage call sites live in patches 0055 (chooser frame) and
0056 (the two dialog doors). Literals are plain ASCII
(const char*), so round23_gate.py searches ASCII, unlike the
UTF-32LE wxString literals of earlier gates.

Modified 2026-11-13 by the KiCad-IOS port (GPLv3 section 5
notice; see MODIFICATIONS.md).

